ন আমার recommendation\nImplementation শুরু করতে পারো, কিন্তু Gemini-কে সরাসরি Step 1–5 execute করতে দিও না।\nপ্রথমে এই Pre-Implementation Gate চালাও:\nAudit গ্রহণযোগ্য এবং architecture direction অনুমোদিত।\nতবে implementation শুরু করার আগে নিচের FINAL CORRECTIONS এবং PRE-IMPLEMENTATION GATES সম্পূর্ণ করো।\n1. Permanent Autonomous Mode\n\"--dangerously-skip-permissions\" আমাদের intentional permanent operating mode।\nএটি:\n- disable করবে না\n- replace করবে না\n- interactive permission workflow ফিরিয়ে আনবে না\n- \"ask\"/\"force_ask\" দিয়ে human approval dependency তৈরি করবে না\nআমাদের model:\n\"AUTONOMOUS EXECUTION + MACHINE POLICY CONTROL\"\n---\n2. PreToolUse-এর সীমা\n\"PreToolUse\"-কে কখনো OS-level security boundary হিসেবে describe করবে না।\nএটি:\n\"Antigravity Application-Level Tool Enforcement\"\nOS-level containment আলাদা layer।\n---\n3. Native Hook Timeout — MUST EXPERIMENTALLY VERIFY\nOfficial documentation দেখে timeout behaviour assume করবে না।\nAGY \"1.2.10\"-এ controlled read-only/sandbox test দিয়ে verify করো:\n1. hook returns allow\n2. hook returns deny\n3. hook crashes\n4. hook returns malformed JSON\n5. hook exceeds configured timeout\n6. hook process is killed\nপ্রতিটির actual result record করো।\nবিশেষ করে:\n\"HOOK TIMEOUT → DENY নাকি TOOL EXECUTION?\"\nএটি প্রমাণ ছাড়া fail-closed দাবি করবে না।\n---\n4. OS Containment MUST BE FIRST-CLASS\nবর্তমান audit-এ যদি সত্যিই:\n\"azureuser → NOPASSWD: ALL\"\nথাকে, তাহলে এটিকে CRITICAL architectural gap হিসেবে রাখো।\nPolicy Gateway alone যথেষ্ট নয়।\nDesign করো:\nHuman/Admin Identity\n≠\nAgent Identity\nAgent identity-এর জন্য minimum privileges:\n- NO sudo\n- NO passwordless root\n- NO Docker privileged access\n- NO access to SSH private keys\n- NO modification of Policy Gateway\n- NO modification of hooks\n- NO modification of safety policy\n- NO modification of other project workspaces\n- NO systemd administration unless explicitly required by a tightly scoped service mechanism\n---\n## 5. Level 2A Definition Tighten করো\n`Single file` alone does NOT make an operation safe.\nLevel 2A requires ALL:\n- single file\n- approved project subtree\n- non-sensitive path\n- non-policy file\n- non-hook file\n- non-secret file\n- non-auth file\n- non-infrastructure file\n- non-dependency file\n- non-schema file\n- validated diff\n- required local test passes\nOtherwise → Level 2B or DENY.\n---\n## 6. Docker Must Be Operation-Aware\nDo not classify all Docker commands as Level 3.\nExamples:\n```text\ndocker ps\ndocker inspect\nmay be read-only.\nBut:\ndocker run -v /:/host\ndocker run --privileged\ndocker exec with host/root access\nmust be hard-denied.\nThe policy must inspect Docker arguments, not only the executable name.\n---\n7. Git Must Be Operation-Aware\nExamples:\ngit status\ngit diff\ngit log\nare read-only.\nPotentially allowed project-local operations may include:\ngit add\ngit commit\nsubject to policy.\nBut autonomous mode must hard-deny:\ngit push\ngit push --force\ngit reset --hard\ngit clean -fd\nunless a future explicit policy changes this.\n---\n8. Policy Self-Protection\nThe gateway MUST protect:\n~/.gemini/config/hooks.json\nAGY-MASTER/POLICIES/\npolicy_gateway.py\nsafety_levels.json\nAGY-MASTER/AGENTS.md\nglobal AGENTS.md\nfrom modification by ordinary project agents.\nDo not rely only on the gateway to protect itself.\nUse filesystem ownership/permissions and separate agent identity where possible.\n---\n9. No Blind Rule Duplication\nBefore modifying project \"AGENTS.md\" files:\nCreate a Rule Distribution Matrix:\nRule\nSource\nGlobal?\nMaster?\nProject?\nDuplicate?\nMissing?\nAuthoritative Location?\nDo not copy the entire 77KB \"AGENTS.md\".\nDo not modify rules merely because they appear in the audit.\nPreserve the existing authoritative meaning.\n---\n10. IMPLEMENTATION ORDER\nAfter the above gates are verified:\nPhase A\nCreate policy gateway + unit tests.\nNO hook activation yet.\nPhase B\nRun adversarial offline tests:\n- unknown agent\n- unknown tool\n- malf